## Rules Maintenance (Meta)

- When changing critical request flows or frontend library usage (e.g., how CSRF headers are sent, how sessions/cookies are handled, or HTTP client patterns), update this frontend rules document with the new canonical approach.
- In Agent mode, ALWAYS review `.cursor/rules/frontend/frontend-rules.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/backend/backend-rules.mdc` before making changes to ensure consistency across frontend and backend.
- For non-GET requests to Rails endpoints protected by CSRF, include `X-CSRF-Token` from the `CSRF-TOKEN` cookie. Always send `credentials: 'include'` so the browser sends the session cookie.
- SPA CSRF bootstrap: Call `GET /api/v1/csrf` first to set `CSRF-TOKEN` cookie before the first POST (login).
- Prefer consistent fetch/HTTP helpers that centralize headers, error handling, and credential behavior (`credentials: 'include'` for session cookies).